---
import ArticleLayout from '../../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import ArticleFaq from '../../../components/ArticleFaq.astro';
import CTASection from '../../../components/CTASection.astro';
import { MANUFACTURER, CERTIFICATIONS, RELATIONSHIP } from '../../../data/site';

const title = 'Battery Quality Control & Testing | Dingwei Battery';
const description = 'How battery quality control works — from incoming material inspection to 100% end-of-line testing and batch traceability — and what buyers should verify.';
const articleTitle = 'Battery quality control and testing';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is battery quality control?', a: 'A four-layer process — incoming material, in-process, end-of-line and batch traceability — that keeps repeat orders matching the approved sample.' },
  { q: 'What tests matter most for a battery?', a: 'CCA (catches a weak cold start), capacity at C20 (catches low stored energy), leak test (catches a case that will lose acid), and open-circuit voltage (catches a cell problem before shipping). Each test catches a different failure, so &ldquo;tested&rdquo; means little unless you know which ones actually ran.' },
  { q: 'Are certifications a guarantee of quality?', a: 'No, but they are a strong signal. Ask for current certificates that cover the specific product rather than marketing claims.' },
];
---
<ArticleLayout title={title} description={description} articleTitle={articleTitle} articleSection="Quality" dateModified="2026-09-03" faqs={faqs}>
  <section class="section container prose">
    <span class="tag">Knowledge · Quality</span>
    <h1>Battery quality control and testing</h1>
    <p class="byline">Published by Dingwei Battery · Last reviewed 2026-09-03 · Source: automotive quality systems</p>
    <p class="lead">Quality control is what makes a repeat order match the approved sample. It runs from incoming material to the last test on the line — and a buyer can verify it without ever visiting the plant.</p>

    <div class="takeaways">
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> Battery quality control spans incoming material inspection, in-process checks, end-of-line electrical testing and batch traceability. A credible supplier can show current certifications and describe the specific tests it runs — not just claim &ldquo;100% quality&rdquo;.
    </div>

    <h2>The four layers of quality control</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>What it checks</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Incoming material</td><td>Lead alloy, paste materials, separators, cases</td><td>Catches input variance before it reaches the line</td></tr>
        <tr><td>In-process</td><td>Curing, pasting, formation parameters</td><td>Keeps every batch within the same process window</td></tr>
        <tr><td>End-of-line</td><td>CCA, capacity, voltage, leak test</td><td>Removes defective units before packing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Batch traceability</td><td>Lot tracking through production</td><td>Isolates a problem to one batch, not the whole order</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>The tests that matter</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>CCA test</strong> — verifies cold-cranking performance against the declared standard (JIS / EN / SAE).</li>
      <li><strong>Capacity test</strong> — verifies the Ah rating at the declared rate (C20).</li>
      <li><strong>Leak test</strong> — confirms the sealed case holds under pressure.</li>
      <li><strong>Voltage check</strong> — confirms a healthy open-circuit voltage before shipping.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Certifications as a proxy for quality</h2>
    <p>Certifications are not a guarantee, but they are a strong signal. {MANUFACTURER.name} holds {CERTIFICATIONS.join(', ')}, which indicate a formal quality management system rather than ad-hoc inspection.</p>
    <p class="note">Ask for <em>current</em> certificates, not marketing claims. A certificate that has expired or does not cover the specific product is not evidence.</p>

    <h2>What buyers should ask</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>What is tested at end-of-line — CCA, capacity, leak, or all three?</li>
      <li>Is every unit tested, or only a sample?</li>
      <li>How is batch traceability maintained?</li>
      <li>Can you provide current certifications that cover this product?</li>
      <li>What is the defect handling and warranty process?</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Connect quality to the physical process in <a href="/knowledge/how-lead-acid-batteries-are-made/">how batteries are made</a>, and to the supplier evaluation in the <a href="/knowledge/oem-battery-supplier-checklist/">supplier checklist</a>.</p>
    <p>{RELATIONSHIP}</p>
    <p><a href="/factory/">Battery factory quality profile &rarr;</a> · <a href="/contact/">Battery quality documentation &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>

  <ArticleFaq faqs={faqs} />

  <CTASection title="Verify quality control with the manufacturer" />
</ArticleLayout>
